{{!
    Overrides the python generator's built-in README.mustache. Passed to the
    generator as -t templates/python; templates absent from that directory fall
    back to the ones embedded in the jar, which is why only this file exists.

    NOTE: a mustache comment ends at its first closing brace pair, so no
    variable or partial tag may appear in this block. Naming one here silently
    ends the comment and renders the remainder as markup.

    Three defects in the built-in template motivated the override:

      - It tells consumers to pip install from git+https against this
        repository. That is private, and even once public it is the wrong way
        to install a published package.
      - It documents `python setup.py install`, removed from setuptools.
      - It advertises pytest to run tests that MANIFEST.in prunes from the
        distribution, so the instruction cannot work for a consumer.

    Deliberately omitted: the generatedDate build-date line, which would churn
    the generated README on every run, and the generatorClass build-package
    line, which leaks an internal Java class name onto the registry page.

    The trailing common_README partial is the generator's own. It carries the
    usage example plus the endpoint, model and authorization tables, all driven
    off the spec -- worth keeping and not worth restating.
}}
